Sval: give each ClearDataService cleaner its own OriginAttributesPattern

deleteDataFromSite handed the caller's pattern object to every cleaner it
runs concurrently. StorageAccessCleaner, ShutdownExceptionsCleaner,
PermissionsCleaner and StoragePermissionsCleaner delete userContextId (and
privateBrowsingId) from it while permissions.isolateBy.userContext is
false, its default. QuotaCleaner.deleteBySite filters origins after an
await, so it read the stripped pattern and cleared the site's storage in
every container. A clear for one container cleared them all, and the
caller's object came back changed. Copying the pattern per cleaner in
deleteDataFromSite fixes every cleaner at once; a chrome-side workaround
needs one call per flag and still shares the object between a flag's
cleaners.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs
index f229ede675..39ea7660e4 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs
@@ -2574,10 +2574,14 @@ ClearDataService.prototype = Object.freeze({
       }
     }
 
+    // Give each cleaner its own copy of the pattern. Some cleaners modify it,
+    // e.g. the permission cleaners strip fields the permission manager doesn't
+    // isolate by, and cleaners run concurrently, so a shared object would leak
+    // those changes into cleaners that read the pattern after an await.
     return this._deleteInternal(aFlags, aCallback, aCleaner =>
       aCleaner.deleteBySite(
         aSchemelessSite,
-        aOriginAttributesPattern,
+        { ...aOriginAttributesPattern },
         aIsUserRequest
       )
     );
